Emetos bundles or ports the third-party material listed below. Each entry names
the step of docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md that adds it; the license text of each asset
is kept in third_party/<name>/ by that step. An entry marked "not yet added" is
planned and has no files in the repository yet.

1. TextMate grammars and language configurations
   Source:  Visual Studio Code, extensions/* (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode)
   License: MIT (Microsoft Corporation) and the license of each grammar's
            upstream project, listed in VS Code's cgmanifest.json files.
   Step 4.6 added Go, JSON (JSON, JSON with Comments, JSON Lines, Code Snippets),
   YAML and Markdown (third_party/vscode-extensions/: VS Code's LICENSE.txt and
   ThirdPartyNotices.txt, which holds the license text of each grammar's
   upstream: go-syntax, vscode-JSON.tmLanguage, better-snippet-syntax,
   YAML-Syntax-Highlighter, vscode-markdown-tm-grammar, all MIT, and the
   TextMate bundle license of markdown.tmbundle, which permits copying, use,
   modification and sale). Step 4.6b added Python (MagicPython, MIT), JavaScript
   and JavaScript React (TypeScript-TmLanguage, MIT, and javascript.tmbundle
   under the TextMate bundle license) and TypeScript and TypeScript React
   (TypeScript-TmLanguage, MIT); their license texts are in the same
   ThirdPartyNotices.txt. Step 4.10 added HTML (html.tmbundle, TextMate bundle
   license), CSS (vscode-css, MIT), SCSS (language-sass, MIT), Less
   (Better-Less, MIT), XML and XSL (language-xml, MIT), SQL (vscode-mssql,
   MIT), Shell Script (better-shell-syntax, MIT), Makefile (make.tmbundle,
   TextMate bundle license), Dockerfile (moby, Apache-2.0) and INI and
   Properties (ini.tmbundle, TextMate bundle license); the texts are in the
   same ThirdPartyNotices.txt, and none was left out. Step 4.11 added C, C++
   and CUDA C++ (better-c-syntax and better-cpp-syntax, MIT; c.tmbundle, TextMate
   bundle license; cuda-cpp-grammar, MIT), Rust (rust-syntax, MIT), Diff
   (diff.tmbundle, TextMate bundle license), Git commit and rebase messages and
   Ignore files (git.tmbundle and git-commit-message-plus, MIT), and the Go
   module, workspace and checksum grammars of golang/vscode-go (MIT; its
   LICENSE is third_party/vscode-go/LICENSE); none was left out.
   A grammar without a permissive license is left out and recorded here.

2. Color themes
   Source:  Visual Studio Code, extensions/theme-defaults
   License: MIT (Microsoft Corporation)
   Added by step 4.7 (internal/core/theme/assets/; the license is in
   third_party/vscode-extensions/). The Dark Modern, Light Modern, Dark+,
   Light+, Dark High Contrast and Light High Contrast themes, and the Visual
   Studio Dark and Light themes that Dark+ and Light+ include.

